---
title: Postmortem Lifecycle
config:
    layout: elk
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB

    [*] --> pending: from process incident-response (incident stabilized)

    pending --> drafting: PM claims postmortem

    drafting --> ready_for_followups: PM completes postmortem narrative

    ready_for_followups --> creating_followups: PM claims for follow-up filing

    creating_followups --> complete: PM files compensating issues (spawn events to process refinement)

    complete --> [*]: terminal (resolved)

    note right of pending
        Cross-process legend:
        • Entry spawn event: from process incident-response. Postmortem is a new work item created when an incident stabilizes; it is not a shared state with incident-response.
        • Exit spawn events: each compensating issue filed during creating_followups is a new raw issue on refinement; those are not shared states either.
        • Exit terminal: complete is internal (meta-work done).
    end note

    note right of drafting
        Working. PM synthesizes the postmortem: summary, timeline, impact, root cause, contributing factors, what worked, what didn't. The responder's root-cause findings are already posted on the incident issue (from the `verifying` phase of incident-response); PM pulls them forward.
    end note

    note right of ready_for_followups
        Resting. Draft is complete; architect reviews for systemic gaps, PO reviews for priority on SEV-1. When review is done, PM reclaims to file follow-ups. Claim SLA: days.
    end note

    note right of creating_followups
        Working. PM reviews the postmortem and files compensating issues — each enters refinement as a raw issue on the refinement lifecycle. Types are typically type:chore (process improvements) and type:bug (latent bugs surfaced).
    end note

    note right of complete
        Terminal (resolved). Postmortem is published and compensating issues are filed. Follow-ups flow through normal refinement and inner loop.
    end note
